{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/390132-what-sort-of-damage-does-your-changelings-do","id":390132,"title":"What sort of damage does your changelings do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T11:42:44-08:00","id":390132,"title":"What sort of damage does your changelings do?","content":"So in my first Changeling chronicle I had a problem with the fact that the Freeholds members didn't do that much bad things against the average mortals in the city. Compared to what a cities vampires would do as part of there power struggles and just feeding that is.<br /> <br /> It didn't feel like proper World of Darkness without it, so I'm wondering: what sort of damage do you imagine that changelings do towards the cities mortal population? Do they hurt their dreams in some way? Do they create widespread fear or support gang wars? And if so why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T12:57:52-08:00","id":390238,"title":"","content":"Why would they be interested in doing any of those things on a scale that actually harms the mortal society they're a part of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:12:45-08:00","id":390248,"title":"","content":"Well I supposed that they would do damage, even if they are not all united in wanting to do it. Much like vampires harm humans without the suffering they inflict being an end unto itself.<br /> <br /> I've always seen that as part of the theme World of Darkness, that the characters, and the NPC:s threaten/disturb the normal world, maybe due to recklessness, maybe due to their own goals conflicting with those of the humans.<br /> <br /> Think about the Silver Ladder, or the Guardians of the Veil in Mage, both of those try to influence or control the mortal world and will likely cause some damage through that right?<br /> <br /> Do you see it differently? Do you envision changelings as neutral or positive for the communities that they live around? Or do you mean that changeling would mostly do things on a personal scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:15:44-08:00","id":390253,"title":"","content":"Changelings tend to be, overall, less a bad thing for a city than Vampires. They are not necessarily a good thing, but as many seem to want to protect humans as exploit them.<br /> <br /> This makes sense, to some degree, with the themes of the game. Vampires are parasites. They take from those around them, and are walking rape metaphors (and sex metaphors, and early homosexuality metaphors, but those are their good points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) . They are, at best, kind of not good things. Almost all vampires kill by feeding sooner or later, and they essentially kill to reproduce. Their help are humans hopelessly addicted to their blood. I won't argue for mass slaughter, but it is hard to say they are not bad things.<br /> <br /> Changelings don't really take any more than humans do. They benifet from emotions on a level humans don't, but don't steal them, though some may spread some misery for darker ones depending. They don't have an innate need to harm those around them, so, like people, some do some don't. Returning to humanity as much as possible is a theme for the game, much like vampires being a predator and struggling to hold onto dwindling humanity is a theme for that one, so they are just different.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:34:17-08:00","id":390391,"title":"","content":"In the setting I made some times ago, I led my players to think that the Courts are the least evil, but still somewhat evil. Spring promote the drugs dealers in the street, harming also children. Summer took over the cops and advocates, freeing criminals to anger the mob. Autumn also help serial killers to escape prison, to propagate fear among the citizens. And Winter hide himself in hospitals, taking care that not every story end well. By doing so they harm innocent people, true, but the generated power blow the Fae away. So, when only bad choices can be made, when every sides are the wrong side, what the players will do ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","user":"Arabidopsis","date":". 02-02-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:10:51-08:00","id":390441,"title":"","content":"You're kind of framing the question as &quot;How do all Changelings in general damage a human population?&quot; I would instead ask &quot;How could a particular Changeling do damage within a human population?&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot more so than in vampire, mage or werewolf settings, individual changelings have their own unique reasons for being messed up and their own methods of being dangerous. A low Clarity ogre is literally hiding under a town bridge and eating every 23rd person who crosses it. A glamour-junkie winter courtier is driving widows to suicide. The Summer King is secretly a loyalist, kidnapping children for his Keeper. A wizened who lives in the park keeps laying curses on anybody who picks the spring flowers.<br /> <br /> In any town that has a reasonable changeling population, Weird Shit will happen far more than usual. Glamour harvesting encourages frequent emotional manipulation of the local mortals, sometimes on a large scale. Courts do vie for earthly influence and resources, on occasion. Loyalists, Bridge-Burners and the Mad all exist, following their individual objectives without much concern for the damage they may cause to others.<br /> <br /> Is your player's particular character a plague on the mortal realm? Not necessarily. He/she probably just wants to live a happy life. The rest of the Freehold, however? The monsters in human guise that only they can recognise and combat? They are capable of causing tremendous amounts of pain and chaos. Many of the Lost are just not as callously indifferent to the pain of those around them than your typical vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T16:47:18-08:00","id":390636,"title":"","content":"I'll agree with the previous posters - on a whole, Changeling society just isn't as predisposed as an institution to abuse humanity as Vampire society is.<br /> <br /> That's because hard-wired into Vampire society is the fact that it's made up of beings that eat humans. If Vampire society ran perfectly, people would still be victimized, because victimizing people is part and parcel of what a vampire is.<br /> <br /> Hard-wired into Changeling society is the fact that it's made up of people who've suffered victimization and, frankly, weren't very fond of it, thanks. If Changeling society ran perfectly, they'd never cause victimization in humans. The Courts and Freehold system are designed, in large part, to *prevent* harm to humans, if only by keeping the attention of the Others away from the area.<br /> <br /> This doesn't necessarily mean that Changelings don't cause victimization in humans, of course. It just means that Changeling society harms mortals when there's a *failure* in the institution - either a failure of conscience (such as when Spring encourages drug use, or Summer riles up gang wars), a failure of insight (such as when they don't realize that one of their own is playing out their own abuses against mortals by kidnapping and eating children), or a failure of effectiveness (when an enemy such as an army of privateers or a vacationing True Fae set up shop to kidnap mortals and the freehold is too weak to usefully oppose them). The World of Darkness being what it is (and Changelings' minds being what *they* are), these failures are common enough to provide plenty of conflict and drama for a good game, in combination of other problems and threats that a Motley of the Lost will face in their day-to-day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:35:48-08:00","id":390700,"title":"","content":"Yeah, changelings as a whole aren't detrimental to the world around them. There's a worrisome implication in the core book about harvesting too much glamour from an individual causing some sort of desensitization but as far as I know it isn't explored further.<br /> <br /> Plus while vampiric power struggles often barge into halls of influence, changeling ones just as often don't go beyond the courts and freeholds.<br /> <br /> However, individuals with power and desperation are another thing.<br /> <br /> Changelings are in hiding, and are probably the safest of supernaturals that we have a larger book of. Trying to influence or control the world can lead to attention being drawn to you. Which can lead to the Things searching for you having that easier a time.<br /> <br /> But there are people willing to take those chances. For instance in the signature city, Miami, the Winter Court acts as an organized crime family. Some might be 'free' of their Keeper, providing they serve up a changeling every year, like the changeling from Hunter, Shakes. Some might just be jerks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:24:56-08:00","id":391049,"title":"","content":"The thing that would scare me most about changelings is the likelihood that they've become more like their abductors: that they've become users and abusers themselves, willing to seduce and deceive and manipulate to get their way. And you can't see them coming \u2014 you can only try to piece things together once they're gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T01:31:38-08:00","id":391151,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the excellent answers!<br /> <br /> Alright, so different changelings might cause damage due to their low Clarity, obsessions or by giving in to parts of their nature and slowly becoming like Keepers themsevles, but it isn't hard-wired into their very existens like with vampires.<br /> <br /> What about the Courts? Do they cause damage (or at least what the mortal world would see as damage) in their struggle to secure the Freehold or stop the Others?<br /> @Arabidopsis, you seemed to say this right? Do the Courst want to foster their dominant feelings within the Freehold, spreading fear, anger etc.<br /> Why? Does that strengthen the Court or the protection of the Freehold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:03:52-08:00","id":391228,"title":"","content":"It depends on the particular freehold and the Lost involved. If the courts don't rotate out but instead must fight for control of the Freehold, then expect to start to see some similar abuses as a Vampire might inflict. Enthralling people, emotional shenanigans and betrayal come with any large scale power structure.<br /> <br /> Even smoothly transitioning Freeholds have Summer Zealots, who rattle sabers and try to raise support for repelling Keepers and elements of the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:26:09-08:00","id":391665,"title":"","content":"There are even Entitlement Orders that certainly fit the mold in terms of unhealthy relationships with humans.<br /> <br /> The Scarecrow Ministry, for example, can sometimes take the extremist position of the Autumn Court, using fear as the only method for interacting with non-changelings. The Duchy of the Icebound Heart are, by far, the most emotionally damaging group of Lost that can exist within a Freehold. There are several other Orders that can take a &quot;means to an end&quot; view of regular people but these ones from the core rulebook spring to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:47:50-08:00","id":391676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Birnam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/390132-what-sort-of-damage-does-your-changelings-do?p=391665#post391665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are even Entitlement Orders that certainly fit the mold in terms of unhealthy relationships with humans.<br /> <br /> The Scarecrow Ministry, for example, can sometimes take the extremist position of the Autumn Court, using fear as the only method for interacting with non-changelings. The Duchy of the Icebound Heart are, by far, the most emotionally damaging group of Lost that can exist within a Freehold. There are several other Orders that can take a &amp;quot;means to an end&amp;quot; view of regular people but these ones from the core rulebook spring to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course, the Ministry is normally an example of how the Courts can have a positive effect, even if they're spreading a normally negative emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:43:58-08:00","id":391766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/390132-what-sort-of-damage-does-your-changelings-do?p=391676#post391676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Of course, the Ministry is normally an example of how the Courts can have a positive effect, even if they're spreading a normally negative emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally. But there's always the one who ends up thinking, &quot;Well, the urban legend will be even more convincing if I kill a guy and leave him crucified in front of the old mansion...&quot;<br /> <br /> Autumn and Winter can sometimes seem like the more callous Courts, due to the emotions they encourage. So you're right to point out the good intentions they are supposed to have: fear keeps people away from danger, sorrow reminds them of important things that have been lost. Any wise Courtier will recognise the utility of their Court's emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T01:48:59-08:00","id":392441,"title":"","content":"The Scarecrow Ministry is a great Entitlement as an example of how changelings can be perciewed as bad guys while having reasons that might be seen as good.<br /> <br /> But is this something that the Courts do systematically as well? Do the Courts traumatize the inhabitants of their city in order to save them from the greater danger of the Others? I've heard this a couple of times (and maybe it's my lack of understanding the world that is the reason I don't already know) but I've never been sure. Do, say, the Summer Court try to spread anger/wrath among the mortals since they believe that this will save the mortals from the Others or improve their way of Life?<br /> <br /> I know that changelings generally tries to invoke their Court feelings to harvets Glamour, but do they try to influence the mortals according to their Court philosophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T12:19:32-08:00","id":392851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Johnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/390132-what-sort-of-damage-does-your-changelings-do?p=392441#post392441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that changelings generally tries to invoke their Court feelings to harvets Glamour, but do they try to influence the mortals according to their Court philosophy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. Well, the Spring Court probably has the most intimate relationship with larger society: their &quot;seize the day&quot; attitude is what makes them the most social and least isolationist court.<br /> <br /> The other courts tend towards a Changeling norm: the feeling of being no longer &quot;human&quot;. Summer is like the soldier who comes home from war, finding that they can no longer relate to the society they've sworn to protect. Autumn knows so much about what's out there and, worse, they start to feel drawn to the alien power of it. Winter wants to hide; humanity makes for a great forest to disappear into but they cannot forget what they've lost and they will not let their guard down enough to integrate fully.<br /> <br /> Sorry, that's me riffing on Court philosophies.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, this all encourages Lost into thinking themselves &quot;othered&quot; to humanity. And with that can come emotional distance.<br /> <br /> As far as encouraging the Court's emotion on a large scale, that's rarer. Unless a very powerful changeling is causing Bedlam, of course. A Court (or that Court's monarch) would need some fairly arcane method of harvesting glamour to benefit the most from constant, widespread emotions. Yeah, a Summer changeling could pick up some easy glamour in a war zone but... war zone. The risks tend to outweigh the benefits.<br /> <br /> To be a Winter courtier for a second, influencing the emotional states of large populations of mortals is also a fantastic way to be noticed by Them. Yes, the Court system is in place to obfuscate the Freehold and each court has an idea for how to deal with the Gentry (&quot;Some ideas better than others,&quot; grumbles the Winter guy.) Turning a town into an orgy-fest in order to gorge on the Glamour, though? The Wyrd and glamour permeating the fabric of the area will be a beacon to the True Fae: they like wild emotions and mortals being used as playthings.<br /> <br /> All this is to say... yeah, I guess it's possible. But it's not how things work best and it's really, really stupid. So it goes back to the failings of individual Lost and how the more sane and sensible members of the Freehold will deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:27:44-08:00","id":393605,"title":"","content":"Okay cool, at least I\u00b4ve gotten that straightened out then.<br /> <br /> Don\u00b4t really know where the expectation came from that the Freeholds presence should be bad for a city of mortals, suppose I figuered it was part of the mood of World of Darkness, still I like that the different templates are different and so I find it refreshing that a community of Lost's affect a city in completely different ways than a group of Kindred.<br /> <br /> Thanks again everyone for the very helpful and clear answers, this has actually left me with some more questions... But those deserve their own threads I think...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:29:20-08:00","id":393930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/390132-what-sort-of-damage-does-your-changelings-do?p=390700#post390700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, changelings as a whole aren't detrimental to the world around them. There's a worrisome implication in the core book about harvesting too much glamour from an individual causing some sort of desensitization but as far as I know it isn't explored further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is fan thing, but I assume the changeling is burning Willpower of mortal when he is Harvesting by Emotions. It would have then sense that is Harvest was big enough ( like 5+ Glamour ), humans would feel burned down by it.<br /> <br /> Not enough to make Lost a monster like Kindred, but enough to mark them as a bit &quot;psychic vampires&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T16:10:31-08:00","id":395546,"title":"","content":"I've never been fond of that houserule. I feel like part of what makes Changeling monsters distinctive is that they aren't inherently monsters - the ones who become monsters, even if they're driven to it, *choose* to be monsters. Making it inherent in the condition dilutes that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T05:06:12-08:00","id":396141,"title":"","content":"Remember. Most changelings are damaged human beings on some level or another. They can become victims as well as monsters. Their addiction to glamor, maybe having a low wyld, there emotional baggage as a whole can make various plot hooks for endangering a city, if not the people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}